  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="182">
        <pb n="231"/>
        <head>182 — i — II. — <quote>Thou hast given a heritage to them that fear thy name</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">On the Holy <persName>Gregory</persName> the Wonder-Worker.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">When the holy apostle was reckoning up in his teaching the riches of the great and superhuman gifts of the Spirit he said, <quote>To that man is given the word of wisdom; and to this<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> the word of knowledge; and to another again the gifts of healings; and to another the performances of wonderful powers<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/></quote>. But <persName>Gregory</persName><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> the servant of God and great and true high-priest, having opened and widened the hidden mouth<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> of his mind, received <pb n="232"/> the divine treasure of these things all together; in that he dried up the lake like <persName>Moses</persName>; and<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> stopped the river and turned it aside like that son of <persName>Nun</persName> <persName>Joshua</persName><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> the general; performed healings and powers like<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> the apostles; and freed<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> peoples and cities from heathen error like <persName>Paul</persName>; [received the knowledge of the true and spotless faith by means of a revelation from heaven : by whose prayers<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/>, <persName>Saviour</persName> of all, have mercy upon us.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 231, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. lxi, 6.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 231, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>another</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 231, n. 4</orig></choice> I Cor. xii, 4-11 <quote>But there are..... in every man. To each man..... itself willeth</quote> (verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 231, n. 5</orig></choice> Marg. <quote>These things about him you will learn from the history of triumphs that <persName>Gregory</persName> of <placeName>Nyssa</placeName> wrote about him</quote> (Migne, <title>P. G.</title> XLVIII, 893 ff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 231, n. 6</orig></choice> Ps. lxxxi, 11 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 232, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>in that he</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 232, n. 2</orig></choice> Corr. <quote><persName>Joshua</persName>; in that he</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 232, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>as</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 232, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>he frees</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 232, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>in that he received the right and unerring faith from heaven (as) a revelation. By his entreaties</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
    </body>
